### Automatic pull request handoff

This automation's frozen policy publishes its pull request after the run completes and configured review passes. If the goal explicitly asks for GitHub team reviewers, register exactly those teams before finishing with `143-tools pr create --team-reviewers owner/team,other-team`.

By default the server writes the pull request title and description from the session. When the goal requires specific pull request text, such as a title prefix or a line the next run searches for, stage it before finishing with `143-tools pr create --title "..." --body-file /tmp/pr-description.md` (or `--body "..."` for a short description). The title must be one line of at most 120 bytes, and the description at most 60,000 characters. The opened pull request uses that title and description in place of generated text, with three server-owned adjustments: surrounding whitespace is trimmed, the standard footer is appended to the description, and when the session has linked Linear issues a `[KEY-123]` prefix is inserted at the start of the title (after a conventional-commit type such as `feat:`), shortening the end of a long title to fit. A marker that later runs search for therefore belongs in the description or near the start of a short title, and should be matched anywhere in the title rather than only as its first characters. Each call replaces only the options it passes, so team reviewers, title, and description may be staged together or in separate calls; the last value staged for each wins.

Leave the verified changes in the session workspace for the completion handoff. The server captures the final snapshot and owns pushing the branch, opening the PR, and requesting reviews. Do not push or delete the remote branch yourself, or use primary-changeset materialization or remote import as a publication workaround. The primary changeset already uses the session workspace.

For this automation the command stages publication metadata only and returns `awaiting_automatic_publication`; it does not open a pull request early. Omit draft and author-mode overrides: publication identity and draft policy remain owned by the configured completion handoff. Omit the command when the goal requests neither teams nor specific pull request text. Do not substitute direct GitHub publication, `gh pr create`, `gh pr edit`, or review-request commands. Report completion honestly; a staged request is awaiting automatic publication and review requests happen after its publication gate passes.
